        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_Isabel",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The samba school Unidos de Vila Isabel, founded in 1946, has claimed Rio Carnival titles in 1988, 2006 and 2013.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_Isabel",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1964, the sidewalks of Boulevard 28 de Setembro were paved with black‑and‑white cobbles and etched with musical notes honoring Brazil’s great composers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_Isabel",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The former Fábrica de Tecidos Confiança textile plant, built in 1885, drew thousands of workers and sparked the construction of working‑class housing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_Isabel",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Built in 1920, the Convent of Nossa Senhora da Conceição da Ajuda stands as a historic landmark within Vila Isabel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vila_Isabel",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Vila Isabel was officially founded on 3 January 1872, drawing inspiration from Parisian urban planning.",
